From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:22:10 +0200
Subject: mtd: devices: qcom_scm_storage: Limit transfers to 64 KiB

Each transfer allocates the data plus a 72 byte header from the SCM tzmem
pool, which is capped at 256 KiB and never shrinks. A 256 KiB chunk rounds
up to 260 KiB and fails with -ENOMEM, so any MTD read or write of 256 KiB
or more breaks. Use 64 KiB chunks to stay well below the pool limit.

Signed-off-by: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
---
 drivers/mtd/devices/qcom_scm_storage.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mtd/devices/qcom_scm_storage.c b/drivers/mtd/devices/qcom_scm_storage.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/mtd/devices/qcom_scm_storage.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/devices/qcom_scm_storage.c
@@ -183,7 +183,8 @@ static int qcom_scm_storage_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	host->buffer_size = SZ_256K;
+	/* Data plus header must fit the 256 KiB SCM tzmem pool */
+	host->buffer_size = SZ_64K;
 	host->buffer = devm_kzalloc(dev, host->buffer_size, GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!host->buffer)
 		return -ENOMEM;
-- 
